<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rangpur (Assam)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rangpur was a capital of the Ahom kingdom, on the outskirts of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sivasagar">Sivasagar</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, not to be confused with Rangpur in Bangladesh. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudra-singha">Rudra Singha</a> in the early eighteenth century, it was the main royal seat for much of that century, when kings built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talatal-ghar">Talatal Ghar</a> palace, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rang-ghar">Rang Ghar</a> pavilion and nearby temples and tanks. Moamoria rebels seized it in 1769, and in 1794 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaurinath-singha">Gaurinath Singha</a> moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jorhat">Jorhat</a>.</p></div>
